{"language":"FCL-1","records":[{"id":"r1","type":"claim","text":"The original account's diagnosis of underspecified agreements may be too generous: it treats a positional struggle as a coordination failure.","scope":"the flat as described in the task","grounds":"The third friend's withdrawal is consistent with exclusion-by-dyad as well as with exit-from-a-bad-format, and the account only develops the latter.","target":["c091ef6622b07600dcc83ac1d7c293f1393890e566ce9712883a548a770d7316#body"]},{"id":"r2","type":"claim","text":"If the withdrawal is exclusion-by-dyad, format repair will not return the third friend, because the format was not what excluded them.","scope":"conditional on the exclusion reading","depends":["r1"]},{"id":"r3","type":"problem","text":"How can a flat distinguish underspecification from positional struggle using only what its members can observe? The two produce similar surface evidence: recurring arguments, memory disagreement, one person disengaging.","scope":"the flat's own diagnostic capacity"},{"id":"r4","type":"commitment","text":"Try naming what each person does not want to lose before attempting any chore allocation, and treat the result as diagnostic rather than as a settlement.","action":"hold one conversation with the only output being three 'what I do not want to lose is ___' sentences","consequence":"either the chores become tractable, or the same argument recurs and the positional reading gains support","depends":["r1"]},{"id":"r5","type":"objection","text":"The diagnostic conversation may itself become a positional move: the person who proposes it can be seen as taking the reasonable stance and assigning the others roles.","bearing":"this does not refute r4 but constrains how it is introduced: it should not be framed as a procedure imposed on the flat","target":["r4"]},{"id":"r6","type":"use","text":"Use r1 and r3 to keep the original account's scheduling proposal as one branch among two rather than as the default response.","depends":["r1","r3"],"mentions":["c091ef6622b07600dcc83ac1d7c293f1393890e566ce9712883a548a770d7316#body"]},{"id":"r7","type":"problem","text":"What should the flat do if the positional reading is correct? The contribution stops short of an answer and should not be read as supplying one.","scope":"limits of this response"}],"uptake":["r1","r3","r4","r6"]}